Original commit body from 1734af01a2f55d801a5cb572984381da130ae33f:

derive_silence_reason gives `unreported` when a pass read files, emitted
nothing, and gave no reason. The linker registry fills files_analyzed from
the read log, so an import probe counts as a read. Only eleven linker bodies
claimed a reason (WI-finij), so unreported was 0 on the self-survey and 4 on
compose-go and 6 on component-model-demo, each a different set (both
reproduced exactly before this change).

Each body below now claims silence_reason_for_candidates(<what its scan
FOUND>), never what it emitted:
- all_calls: http, graphql, subprocess;
- all_patterns: websocket, event-sourcing, database-query, phoenix-ipc;
- argparse-dispatch: set_defaults registrations;
- go-cobra: cobra.Command handler assignments;
- go-memberlist: files that use memberlist, set before its early returns;
- lua-ffi: phase-1 FFI calls;
- napi: exports;
- ruby-ffi: FFI calls plus rb_define sites.

Analyzers: base.claim_declaration_silence(run, declared, symbols, edges).
An analyzer's emission is the declarations its scan finds, so a silent run
read files and declared nothing (no_candidate_construct), or declared and
then dropped all of it in post-processing (candidates_unresolved). The base
pipeline passes its pass-1 symbols. c (symbols before its declaration merge),
json, proto, vue and latex call the helper from their own analyze().

Measured after:
- A construct-free file in every language a pass reads (plus a C function
  and a .tex), --frameworks all: 16 unreported -> 0
  (test_pass_silence_claims).
- compose-go 4 -> 0, component-model-demo 6 -> 0, flask-restful 0,
  gin-realworld 0, cowboy 0, confluent-examples 0. cowboy (latex) and
  confluent-examples (napi, ruby-ffi) surfaced after the first eleven were
  fixed; they are covered here.
- Dropping http's, napi's or ruby-ffi's claim reds the enumerating test,
  naming that pass.
- Targeted tests: a found-but-unresolved construct (argparse handler,
  cobra handler, memberlist import with no delegate) is
  candidates_unresolved.

NOT asserted: the general claim for the ~50 linker bodies that still make no
claim. Those read no file before finding a candidate, so the orchestrator's
no_candidate_files covers them on every corpus measured; a repository whose
mix reaches a new file-reading branch can still produce `unreported`.

